1
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:11,120
Lighten up and give it a try, will you?

2
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:24,280
Anyone who's broke, come to me!

3
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:29,000
I'm broke too, so don't worry about it!

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,820
Look at the blue sky,

5
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:36,300
white clouds.

6
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:42,840
Things'll work out somehow, eventually.

7
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,900
Anyone without a job, come to me!

8
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,560
I don't have one either, so don't you worry!

9
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:43,460
I'll teach you how to keep pets.

10
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:48,460
I see.

11
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:52,880
Don't stand behind me.

12
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:56,300
Sorry, that was Bolbo-san's tea.

13
00:01:57,420 --> 00:01:58,500
It's Reiko-san.

14
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:01,060
Honestly, Bolbo has such a big body,

15
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:03,400
but without a weapon,
he has the heart of a flea.

16
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:05,940
It's not like I'm scared or anything.

17
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:09,860
I just still can't shake the
habits from my Green Beret days.

18
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:12,520
Which came first, the chicken or the egg?

19
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:17,060
To hide my own cowardice,

20
00:02:17,060 --> 00:02:19,340
I train my body,

21
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:22,220
and the people who arm themselves

22
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:25,460
are plenty.

23
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:30,860
Knock it off already.

24
00:02:30,860 --> 00:02:32,580
That's my line.

25
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:38,120
It's your cell phone.

26
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,360
Right.

27
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:43,220
I've got an email from Jodie.

28
00:02:43,220 --> 00:02:45,020
She's already arrived in Japan?

29
00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:46,620
My darling Bobby,

30
00:02:46,620 --> 00:02:49,120
I have a favor to ask of you today, Bobby.

31
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:51,020
I'm coming over to see you now.

32
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:52,800
Because, Ryotsu...

33
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:55,200
Jodie says she has a favor to ask me.

34
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:56,300
I wonder what it could be.

35
00:02:57,740 --> 00:02:59,340
How would I know that?

36
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:02,720
Ever since I met Jodie...

37
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:09,380
Maybe the time has finally
come to make a decision.

38
00:03:10,140 --> 00:03:10,920
Bobby

39
00:03:11,380 --> 00:03:14,420
I tried making nikujaga
with a Japanese twist,

40
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:15,760
would you give it a taste?

41
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:17,060
Ahh~n

42
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:18,880
Ahh~n

43
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:22,220
It's delicious, Jodie!

44
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:23,740
Welcome, Bobby!

45
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:24,640
It's Jodie!

46
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:28,240
He's getting a nosebleed
just from hearing her voice.

47
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:31,280
If he gets married, he'll definitely die.

48
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:32,140
Bobby

49
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:32,700
Yes?

50
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:34,240
Bobby, wait!

51
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:34,780
Yes?

52
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:40,100
Alright, everyone.
Jodie-san, he's been waiting for you.

53
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:40,880
Jodie.

54
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:43,200
I missed you, Bobby, woof.

55
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:46,380
Jodie.

56
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:50,680
Is this Jodie's Doberman?

57
00:03:51,740 --> 00:03:53,420
Yes. I just started keeping him recently.

58
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:56,900
He's a two-year-old male,
and his name is Bobby.

59
00:03:58,440 --> 00:03:59,975
Yes, I gave him the same name.

60
00:04:00,025 --> 00:04:02,800
That way you won't feel lonely
when you can't see Bobby, right?

61
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:04,220
Jodie.

62
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:07,520
Look at him, happy that a dog got his name.

63
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:12,260
He's well trained, isn't he?
Such a good boy.

64
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:13,620
He really does look like Bobby.

65
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:19,240
I thought I'd get a long break this time,
so I brought her along, but

66
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:25,000
suddenly I've been added to a
month-long public training, Bobby.

67
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,660
So the favor is...

68
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:33,100
Actually, while I'm at training,
I need you to look after her.

69
00:04:35,980 --> 00:04:39,960
She's well trained,
so I don't think she'll cause any trouble.

70
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,340
Could you do that for me, Bobby?

71
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:45,360
Got it, Jodie. No problem at all.

72
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:46,800
Thanks, Bobby!

73
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:53,720
I've already sent her
things to Bobby's apartment.

74
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:55,960
Then I'm counting on you.

75
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:00,100
Bye-bye, Bobby!

76
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:10,260
At this rate, nikujaga's a long way off.

77
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:12,900
Jodie

78
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:26,340
Seeing how happy Jodie was, I just couldn't
bring myself to tell her my condo bans pets.

79
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:32,080
Bobby, stop, stay, sit!

80
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,760
Manager-san

81
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:38,100
Hello.

82
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:43,180
Bolbo-san, welcome home.

83
00:05:47,140 --> 00:05:48,440
What's that, then?

84
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:51,380
A friend gave me some fresh spiny lobsters.

85
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:52,920
That many?

86
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:55,540
Yes, they're quite good ones. Well, then.

87
00:05:55,540 --> 00:05:57,040
Bolbo-san.

88
00:05:58,020 --> 00:06:00,400
We're holding a delivery for you.

89
00:06:04,340 --> 00:06:06,600
It looks just like a pile of moving boxes.

90
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:10,540
It's probably something my
mom sent from the countryside.

91
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:15,140
Thank you very much.

92
00:06:20,620 --> 00:06:21,760
Bobby

93
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:24,320
Bobby

94
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:29,020
Sorry for making you feel cooped up.

95
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:31,200
But I had no choice.

96
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:33,380
This condo bans pets,

97
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:36,460
so keep quiet, okay?

98
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:39,220
If the neighbors find out,
we'll both be kicked out.

99
00:06:42,180 --> 00:06:43,060
Food?

100
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:44,560
You're hungry Bobby?

101
00:06:45,460 --> 00:06:46,740
Alright, hang on a sec.

102
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:49,240
Where's the food?

103
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:02,060
Look, Bobby, it looks tasty, doesn't it?

104
00:07:06,920 --> 00:07:09,660
What's wrong? Aren't you hungry?

105
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:15,140
I don't get it. What are you trying to say?

106
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:18,440
I see. It's hard to
eat straight from the can

107
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:22,860
There, this should do, right?

108
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:26,620
Still something missing?

109
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:29,320
Do you want chopsticks or something?

110
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:40,300
So you always eat off this plate?

111
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:41,440
How fancy.

112
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:45,780
Finally, you're eating.

113
00:07:45,780 --> 00:07:49,716
Hmm, but pet supplies are
so luxurious these days.

114
00:07:49,766 --> 00:07:51,760
Even dog futons, no less.

115
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:54,440
Alright, your bed's ready, Bobby.

116
00:07:56,920 --> 00:08:00,060
Bobby, your futon is over here.

117
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:05,344
Hey, get down.

118
00:08:05,394 --> 00:08:09,080
I've barely said this is
my bed and you're already -

119
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:11,700
What are you doing?
I told you, this one's mine.

120
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:16,580
I already told you, it's mine!

121
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:19,980
Hey, come on!

122
00:08:19,980 --> 00:08:21,180
Damn it.

123
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:25,760
Hey, you

124
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:28,980
what do you think you're doing

125
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:29,500
Hey!

126
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:31,140
I told you to keep watch

127
00:08:31,140 --> 00:08:32,260
what's wrong

128
00:08:32,260 --> 00:08:33,700
what were you doing?

129
00:08:33,700 --> 00:08:34,080
Hey!

130
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:42,120
Fine, I get it.

131
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:45,640
But just tonight.
From tomorrow, it's downstairs.

132
00:08:46,540 --> 00:08:48,000
What are you doing, Bobby?

133
00:08:50,140 --> 00:08:53,840
What a naughty boy.
Jodie will be sad, Bobby.

134
00:08:56,620 --> 00:08:57,680
Bolbo-san

135
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:00,400
Manager.

136
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:05,260
Some neighbors said
they heard a dog barking.

137
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:06,760
Coming!

138
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:10,940
Damn, if they see this, I'm done for.

139
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:15,060
Bobby!

140
00:09:16,140 --> 00:09:19,900
Bobby! That's dangerous,
so let's swap it for this one!

141
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:22,480
Look, a ball! You like that

142
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:26,300
Bobby!

143
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:45,440
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeh!

144
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:46,180
Only for me

145
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:48,500
Come in.

146
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:52,720
Bobby...

147
00:09:55,700 --> 00:10:00,840
Ahhhhhhhhhhhhhh...
I thought Bobby was a toy.

148
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:04,720
It was my fault for not
putting my weapons away properly.

149
00:10:05,540 --> 00:10:10,720
What a cheeky-looking dog.
Apparently Jodie was putting on an act.

150
00:10:11,540 --> 00:10:14,760
Senpai, please hurry up and
do something about this too.

151
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:18,220
Hey, stop wandering around and sit.

152
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:19,320
Sit.

153
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:26,000
Are you saying this
bastard's too filthy to sit?

154
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:28,520
Face forward.

155
00:10:28,520 --> 00:10:31,500
Bobby, come on, sit right here.

156
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:40,260
Listen, dogs like Bobby,
once they see you're weaker than them,

157
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:42,600
they get the idea they're the boss.

158
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:46,080
If you're the owner, act like one.
Be firm and strong.

159
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:47,120
Sorry.

160
00:10:47,660 --> 00:10:50,560
But when I think about how he's
lonely after parting with Jodie,

161
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:52,440
I just can't bring myself
to be strict with him.

162
00:10:53,300 --> 00:10:55,760
That's one thing, and this is another.

163
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:57,440
Letting him do whatever he likes,

164
00:10:57,440 --> 00:11:00,220
in the end,
it's the pet who suffers, you know.

165
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:07,240
Senpai

166
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:09,620
I'm not good with dogs.

167
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:12,380
Pets are banned here too, right?

168
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:20,220
Bobby's getting away!

169
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:27,100
Nikoniko Dorm bans pets!

170
00:11:28,620 --> 00:11:29,460
Wait!

171
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:35,400
Hey, wait!

172
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:39,740
Bobby!

173
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:44,640
Which way did he go?

174
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:45,640
This way!

175
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:51,440
That's Jodie's dog!

176
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:52,460
You're right.

177
00:12:04,740 --> 00:12:06,020
So this is where you are.

178
00:12:06,620 --> 00:12:10,020
Ryo-san, what's going on at this hour?

179
00:12:10,420 --> 00:12:11,960
Don't ask.

180
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:12,600
Bobby.

181
00:12:13,260 --> 00:12:15,300
I'm scared, too. So scared.

182
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:17,480
Is that so?

183
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:21,860
Honestly, Bolb's gone and
saddled me with this crazy pet.

184
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:26,860
Jodie won't be back for a while, Bobby.

185
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:30,140
Yes, Jodie.

186
00:12:30,140 --> 00:12:32,920
Hello, Bobby.

187
00:12:33,540 --> 00:12:35,200
Are you two being good?

188
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:37,060
I'll miss you.

189
00:12:38,220 --> 00:12:40,380
Don't worry about Bobby.

190
00:12:40,380 --> 00:12:43,140
Don't worry,
and good luck with your training.

191
00:12:43,140 --> 00:12:45,240
Hey, Bobby, it's Jodie!

192
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,400
Pop!

193
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:48,340
Yeah, got it.

194
00:12:48,340 --> 00:12:50,080
Well, bye, Jodie.

195
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:53,160
What's all this
"don't worry," you homeless mutt?

196
00:12:53,160 --> 00:12:56,380
Gyaaah, what am I supposed to do?

197
00:12:56,380 --> 00:12:57,680
Don't ask me.

198
00:12:57,680 --> 00:13:00,100
How about here?

199
00:13:01,860 --> 00:13:04,380
This is the condo near the station
where you can live with pets, right?

200
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:06,660
Pet condo.

201
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:14,180
Where's the owner's room?

202
00:13:14,740 --> 00:13:15,580
Is it here?

203
00:13:15,580 --> 00:13:16,260
Yes.

204
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:19,800
Can I help you?

205
00:13:20,380 --> 00:13:23,040
Actually, I'd like to move into this condo.

206
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:24,240
I understand.

207
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:26,440
I'm a bit busy right now,

208
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:29,540
could you come up to my
room on the top floor?

209
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:34,820
Please bring your pet along too.

210
00:13:50,380 --> 00:13:52,040
What a luxurious place!

211
00:13:52,040 --> 00:13:52,340
What's wrong, Bee?

212
00:13:52,940 --> 00:13:55,460
Look, there are lots of friends here too.

213
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:56,140
Look.

214
00:13:58,120 --> 00:14:01,600
There's even a pet shop and a
convenience store that only sells pet food!

215
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:04,780
It really is a condo made for pets.

216
00:14:04,780 --> 00:14:07,520
Here, you can keep Bobby
without any worries, right?

217
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:09,480
Bobby, look, what are you scared of?

218
00:14:09,940 --> 00:14:10,320
This one.

219
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:13,800
Isn't that a horse?

220
00:14:14,260 --> 00:14:18,280
I hear the pets kept in this
condo aren't just dogs and cats

221
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:21,180
No way.

222
00:14:23,380 --> 00:14:25,760
You're the one who's way more dangerous.

223
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:28,240
A new face.

224
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:31,440
What are you doing in a place like this?

225
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,000
Well, just

226
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,920
Excuse me, where's the elevator?

227
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:38,420
There isn't one, dear.

228
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:41,340
If a pet got caught in it,
it would be terrible, wouldn't it?

229
00:14:41,340 --> 00:14:43,060
No elevator?

230
00:14:43,060 --> 00:14:45,340
In a building this big?

231
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:53,020
So they go back and
forth on that slope, then?

232
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:58,560
This condo was designed with the animals' needs first and foremost,
you know.

233
00:14:58,560 --> 00:14:59,560
Wonderful.

234
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:01,760
By the way, where's Bobby?

235
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:06,300
Way over there, like that.

236
00:15:06,300 --> 00:15:10,520
They say pets start to look like their owners,
but isn't that too quick?

237
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:15,300
Amazing.

238
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:19,300
With this, pets can get plenty of
exercise without ever going outside!

239
00:15:23,020 --> 00:15:25,740
Why is a Doberman getting
distracted by a Chihuahua?

240
00:15:25,740 --> 00:15:28,980
It's looking more and more like its owner,
all zutai and no brains.

241
00:15:30,020 --> 00:15:34,500
It's just excited from seeing so many animals all at once,
right, Bobby?

242
00:15:37,460 --> 00:15:38,180
Bobby!

243
00:15:38,180 --> 00:15:43,000
Bobby ran off!

244
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:44,780
2

245
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:49,640
Usoyori-chan!

246
00:15:53,340 --> 00:15:56,020
Who let a dog into the second floor?

247
00:15:56,020 --> 00:15:58,900
Sorry, that's my dog.

248
00:15:58,900 --> 00:16:01,820
The rule is that dogs and cats
stay on the first floor, right?

249
00:16:09,680 --> 00:16:11,320
Are you sure it's this way?

250
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,580
It's suddenly gotten hot.

251
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:18,480
Past here is the tropical animal zone,
you know.

252
00:16:26,980 --> 00:16:28,300
What the hell is this?

253
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:33,940
The third-floor hallway's been turned into
a river for the water-dwelling animals.

254
00:16:34,580 --> 00:16:36,180
You should have said that first!

255
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:41,760
Right, the slope on the right!

256
00:16:41,760 --> 00:16:43,780
Sayuri-chan ran off to the fourth floor.

257
00:16:51,380 --> 00:16:52,780
Grandfather!

258
00:17:00,300 --> 00:17:02,280
So that crocodile was a pet too?

259
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:04,040
At least we're safe for now.

260
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:05,940
That's what we thought,
but it didn't last long.

261
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:07,160
A waterfall!

262
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:24,260
Oh my, what are you doing over there?

263
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:26,060
Nothing really.

264
00:17:27,300 --> 00:17:30,620
That's right. I hear there's a
lost Doberman on the fourth floor.

265
00:17:30,620 --> 00:17:32,600
It isn't your dog, is it?

266
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:35,400
Bobby... on the fourth floor, you say?

267
00:17:36,520 --> 00:17:38,440
You should be worried about me too!

268
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:40,200
Bobby!

269
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:41,120
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

270
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:43,700
Bobby, this way!

271
00:17:45,620 --> 00:17:47,340
This door is awfully heavy.

272
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:53,280
What on earth is this place?

273
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:55,400
Are we at the North Pole or the South Pole?

274
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:59,120
It's freezing! The AC is way too strong!

275
00:18:01,460 --> 00:18:04,620
Keeping a todoma as a pet is going too far!

276
00:18:04,620 --> 00:18:06,860
Stay alive, Bobby!

277
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,480
Someone's collapsed over there!

278
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:12,640
Hey, are you all right?

279
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:15,100
It's the delivery man
from Tsurukame Prefecture!

280
00:18:15,100 --> 00:18:18,080
Come on, pull yourself together!
If you fall asleep, you'll die!

281
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:22,060
Ryo-san,
when I came to deliver your order...

282
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:27,540
I'll be right back to
Mr. Tsurukame-ken. Suzuki

283
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:28,960
You carefree fool.

284
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:31,140
It's turned into frozen ramen.

285
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:34,640
"Then let's just pop it in the microwave,"
is no time for jokes.

286
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:36,660
At this rate, we'll freeze to death!

287
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:38,600
Sorry.

288
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:41,060
Are you Mr. Suzuki?

289
00:18:42,380 --> 00:18:45,200
Yes, I was going to the convenience
store downstairs to buy penguin food.

290
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:47,880
An ambulance comes before penguin food!

291
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:48,760
Y-yes.

292
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:50,980
Bobby, Bobby.

293
00:18:52,100 --> 00:18:55,740
What's next?
Come at me from anywhere, I'm ready for it!

294
00:18:56,180 --> 00:18:58,540
Whoa, what are you all?

295
00:18:58,540 --> 00:18:59,600
Looks like Ruijin-enku.

296
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:03,600
I'm not your parent! Get off me!

297
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:06,140
Something's coming!

298
00:19:09,040 --> 00:19:10,020
How is it?

299
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:11,460
I'm going to be crushed.

300
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:16,440
Saved!

301
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:19,940
What now?

302
00:19:22,260 --> 00:19:23,980
Thank goodness you're safe.

303
00:19:23,980 --> 00:19:26,060
Aren't you the one from earlier?

304
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:27,480
Excuse me.

305
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:31,020
Have you seen my Bobby?

306
00:19:31,680 --> 00:19:33,040
I don't know.

307
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:37,720
Isn't it? What's upstairs, then?

308
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:41,140
The floor above this is already the nineteenth.
The nineteenth!

309
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:43,520
Bobby, wait! Volvo!

310
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:46,000
You'd better call for
backup and come back later.

311
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:49,800
I'm going to look for Bobby.
If you want to go home, go alone.

312
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:55,420
Well then,
I'll take you up on that, Ryo-chan.

313
00:19:55,420 --> 00:19:59,080
If it's hell whether we go forward or back,
I'll just fall face-first.

314
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:10,720
Is this a safari park or what?

315
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:13,980
Even if they're wild beasts,
they're supposed to be pets, at least.

316
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:17,160
Okay, everyone, good kids, good kids!

317
00:20:19,380 --> 00:20:21,820
More like invincible guard dogs than pets.

318
00:20:25,980 --> 00:20:26,960
Bobby.

319
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:29,640
No, Volvo.

320
00:20:44,020 --> 00:20:45,980
Bobby, run!

321
00:20:47,820 --> 00:20:49,650
Run, Bobby!

322
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:53,400
Bobby!

323
00:20:54,180 --> 00:20:57,857
I'm warning you,
I haven't bathed in a month.

324
00:20:57,907 --> 00:20:59,460
Don't blame me if you get an upset stomach.

325
00:21:01,380 --> 00:21:02,820
Karon, Jiro, attack!

326
00:21:07,280 --> 00:21:09,100
If you're here to sell something, no thanks.

327
00:21:09,320 --> 00:21:10,640
Is that your lion?

328
00:21:11,140 --> 00:21:14,514
I've raised him since he was a cub,
so he's used to people,

329
00:21:14,564 --> 00:21:17,560
but I've trained him to
bark at suspicious visitors.

330
00:21:18,980 --> 00:21:21,200
Ordinary people could never
get close to a lion like that.

331
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:25,560
So you accept me?

332
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:32,340
I held my own against the king of beasts.

333
00:21:32,340 --> 00:21:33,540
Of course.

334
00:21:33,540 --> 00:21:35,720
Ryotsu, how did you

335
00:21:35,720 --> 00:21:38,140
...probably only eat the good stuff, right?

336
00:21:38,140 --> 00:21:39,900
Such weaklings.

337
00:21:42,420 --> 00:21:45,080
If you two aren't salesmen,

338
00:21:45,080 --> 00:21:46,860
then what did you come all this way for?

339
00:21:46,860 --> 00:21:48,800
I almost forgot.

340
00:21:48,800 --> 00:21:50,480
Where's the owner's room?

341
00:22:02,180 --> 00:22:03,020
Well, this is something.

342
00:22:03,020 --> 00:22:04,980
Where's the owner?

343
00:22:08,120 --> 00:22:09,080
Welcome!

344
00:22:09,080 --> 00:22:12,380
Did you like my pet-friendly condo?

345
00:22:13,320 --> 00:22:15,020
Well, I mean...

346
00:22:15,020 --> 00:22:18,200
Making it here alive feels like a dream.

347
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:20,520
You still aren't impressed?

348
00:22:20,960 --> 00:22:23,880
Then allow me to show you the rooftop,
my pride and joy.

349
00:22:35,580 --> 00:22:37,140
This is my ranch.

350
00:22:37,140 --> 00:22:40,020
It's been my dream since I was a child.

351
00:22:40,020 --> 00:22:43,760
Why force something like this
into the middle of the city?

352
00:22:43,760 --> 00:22:46,000
Why not just live in the countryside?

353
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:48,940
I was born and raised in Tokyo.

354
00:22:48,940 --> 00:22:51,560
I can't give up the
convenience of city life.

355
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:55,800
Ryotsu, I'm sorry, after you went to
all the trouble of looking after things,

356
00:22:56,240 --> 00:23:00,520
but I think Bobby and I should
live where there's real nature.

357
00:23:01,580 --> 00:23:05,320
I've come to feel that's
best for Bobby, too.

358
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:08,340
I think that's better too, Bobby.

359
00:23:08,340 --> 00:23:11,500
You've become a proper owner for Bobby.

360
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:17,660
It's an emergency escape chute for animals.

361
00:23:17,660 --> 00:23:18,380
What is this?

362
00:23:33,040 --> 00:23:34,800
Hi there, Bobby!

363
00:23:34,800 --> 00:23:36,640
Jody, what are you doing here?

364
00:23:37,060 --> 00:23:40,100
Our ship's engine trouble
delayed our departure.

365
00:23:40,100 --> 00:23:41,800
So I'm on temporary leave until then.

366
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:44,460
Really, Jody?

367
00:23:45,420 --> 00:23:46,320
Bobby!

368
00:23:46,900 --> 00:23:49,440
Come on, Bobby, let's go on vacation!

369
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:51,040
Vacation?

370
00:23:52,800 --> 00:23:54,120
Jody!

371
00:23:54,700 --> 00:23:57,420
Bobby, where on earth are we going?

372
00:23:57,980 --> 00:24:00,440
Ask the sheep.

373
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:20,240
Like the rain-washed day that
seems to be calling out to me

374
00:24:21,640 --> 00:24:24,500
I walked on, looking back

375
00:24:24,500 --> 00:24:27,100
Led by the hand of the clatter

376
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:34,240
That strange feeling I had back then

377
00:24:35,500 --> 00:24:39,520
So on the tiles of the arcade street

378
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:45,280
I tried walking only on the black ones

379
00:24:47,860 --> 00:24:53,420
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten

380
00:24:54,580 --> 00:24:57,580
Not for the politicians with
their self-important faces

381
00:24:57,580 --> 00:25:00,900
Nor for the aunties with blue eyeshadow

382
00:25:01,420 --> 00:25:06,480
Why not turn at that corner over there

383
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:11,680
I'll get to meet everyone,

384
00:25:14,020 --> 00:25:16,560
over there in Kameari,

385
00:25:17,500 --> 00:25:20,100
well, surely in Kameari,

386
00:25:21,140 --> 00:25:24,880
everyone, come on over to our town!

387
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:26,360
Thank you.

388
00:25:30,140 --> 00:25:34,240
Isn't that the armored traffic safety
old guy from the Nishitsu Railway?

389
00:25:34,240 --> 00:25:36,900
They took his sworn patrol light?

390
00:25:37,140 --> 00:25:39,640
And on top of that,
the old man's a total dimwit?

391
00:25:40,200 --> 00:25:43,080
Looks like this guy's got quite the story.

392
00:25:43,080 --> 00:25:47,420
Next time, the traffic safety demon's back,
so look out for him.

393
00:25:52,560 --> 00:25:53,040
Thank you.

